# =============================================================================
# Trades Journal — Environment Template
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev:   cp .env.example .env.local
# `.env.local` is gitignored — it MUST never be committed.
# In production, inject these via the platform secret store, NOT a file:
#   - Vercel:  Project → Settings → Environment Variables
#   - CI/CD:   GitHub Actions → repo Secrets (referenced as ${{ secrets.* }})
#   - Self-host / Docker: Vault / Doppler / SOPS-encrypted, mounted at runtime
# Separation of code and configuration is enforced by design: no secret value
# is ever hardcoded in source. Every consumer reads from `process.env`.
# =============================================================================

# --- Supabase: Postgres + Auth backend ---------------------------------------
# Project Dashboard → Settings → API.
# The ANON / publishable key is row-level-security (RLS) scoped and safe to ship
# to the browser. Access is governed by RLS policies, not key secrecy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-publishable-key

# --- Supabase: Server-only admin key -----------------------------------------
# Bypasses RLS. NEVER expose to the client and NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Only set if a trusted server task genuinely needs to bypass row security.
# Leave empty unless required.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Public site URL ----------------------------------------------------------
# Used to build OAuth redirect callbacks. Must match the URL the app is served
# from, or the OAuth provider will reject the redirect.
#   Local:       http://localhost:3000
#   Production:   https://your-deployment.vercel.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Google OAuth (optional) --------------------------------------------------
# Configured in Supabase: Authentication → Providers → Google.
# Listed here for reference; values live in the Supabase dashboard, not here.
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
